<title>USA: Continued fair skies for Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</title>
<headline>Continued fair skies for Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Warm, high pressure aloft over Brazil's coffee belt is expected to remain in place for the next seven days preventing any cold air from moving into the area, Weather Services Corp said an update on Monday.</p>
<p>The weekend saw fair skies over most main growing areas of the belt. Temperatures remained near normal levels with lows in the 50's F (10-15 C). Some higher elevations reported cooler conditions.</p>
<p>Fair to partly cloudy skies are expected for the next week. Temperatures should remain near to above normal levels for this time of year. Low temperatures are expected to be in the 50's to low 60's F (low to middle teens C).</p>
<p>&quot;There is no damaging cold expected,&quot; WSC said.</p>
<p>((--New York Commodity Desk 212 859-1640))</p>
